conversations, who are interested in nuance, who are interested in what their own minds are doing, who are interested in how they can modify and change how their thinking and how they should be responding to the world to have better relationships or perform better or function better at work or in their lives. That audience turns out not to be trivial. It turns out to be substantial. So, you know, I would say the short answer to your question, Kim, is that that you know, the short answer really to how anyone gets successful, which is they work very hard and most of it is luck.

